    <h1>Mod loading: <span class="docs-accent">what works today</span></h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        This page is intentionally explicit about the difference between existing SDK contracts and a complete mod runtime. It prevents mod authors from following a workflow the repository does not implement yet.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-status-grid">

        <div class="docs-status-item">
            <span class="docs-status status-present">PRESENT</span>
            <strong>SDK contracts</strong>
            <p>
                IMod, IModContext, logger, block and item registries, and world-generation interfaces exist.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-status-item">
            <span class="docs-status status-present">PRESENT</span>
            <strong>Built-in MainMod</strong>
            <p>
                The game creates and initializes its own content mod directly.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-status-item">
            <span class="docs-status status-missing">NOT IMPLEMENTED</span>
            <strong>External assembly loader</strong>
            <p>
                No external assembly discovery/loading pipeline is present in this snapshot.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-status-item">
            <span class="docs-status status-missing">PLACEHOLDER</span>
            <strong>Crafty.MDK</strong>
